r {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "17 – 20 July 1924"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/265"} "Stade Yves-de-Manoir, Colombes"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/70067"} "70 from 9 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Placement determined by best scores on apparatus in individual all-around event."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Until the late 1970s, it was very rare for American gymnasts to be competitive at the international level. Their only Olympic gold medals until then occurred at the " [:a {:href "/editions/3/sports/GAR"} "1904"] " and " [:a {:href "/editions/10/sports/GAR"} "1932 Olympics"] ", held on US soil – with one exception, this event. " [:a {:href "/athletes/31368"} "Frank Kriz"] " was completely unknown in Europe, but won the horse vault narrowly over Czechoslovakian " [:a {:href "/athletes/31174"} "Jan Koutný"] ". Kriz finished only 19th in the " [:a {:href "/results/70062"} "individual all-around"] ", and made the top 10 only in " [:a {:href "/results/70073"} "rope climbing"] " and on the " [:a {:href "/results/70072"} "side horse"] ", other than the horse vault. He was helped because the event was not held under standard international rules, but was more of a high jump- or high vault-type event. Kriz also competed at the Olympics in " [:a {:href "/results/70058"} "1920"] " and 1928. Before 1976, the only other USA gymnastic medal at a non-domestic Olympics would come when the " [:a {:href "/results/70149"} "women’s team"] " won a bronze medal in 1948. Koutný competed at the 1928 Olympics, where he won a silver medal in the " [:a {:href "/results/70075"} "team event"] ", but this was his only individual Olympic medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td